/* book Worked example: Q: An air standard Dual cycle has a compression ratio of 14. At the start of compression the air is at 1 bar and 300 K. The pressure ratio during constant-volume heat addition is 1.5 and the cut-off ratio is 1.6. Take cp = 1.005, cv = 0.718, R = 0.287 kJ/kg·K and γ = 1.4. Find the temperatures, the heat added and rejected, the efficiency and the mean effective pressure.
   1. T₂ = 300 × 140.4 = 300 × 2.874 = 862.1 K; p₂ = 141.4 = 40.23 bar.
   2. Constant volume: T₃ = 1.5 × 862.1 = 1293.2 K and p₃ = 1.5 × 40.23 = 60.35 bar (the peak pressure).
   3. Constant pressure: T₄ = 1.6 × 1293.2 = 2069.1 K (the peak temperature).
   4. Expansion to v₅ = v₁: T₅ = T₁rprcγ = 300 × 1.5 × 1.931 = 868.9 K.
   5. qin = 0.718 × (1293.2 − 862.1) + 1.005 × (2069.1 − 1293.2) = 309.5 + 779.8 = 1089.3 kJ/kg.
   6. qout = 0.718 × (868.9 − 300) = 408.5 kJ/kg; wnet = 1089.3 − 408.5 = 680.8 kJ/kg; η = 680.8/1089.3 = 0.625. The formula gives the same 0.625.
   7. v₁ = 0.287 × 300/100 = 0.861 m³/kg; v₂ = 0.861/14 = 0.0615 m³/kg. pm = 680.8/(0.861 − 0.0615) = 851.6 kPa = 8.52 bar.
   Answer: T₂ = 862.1 K, T₃ = 1293.2 K, T₄ = 2069.1 K, T₅ = 868.9 K; qin = 1089.3 kJ/kg, qout = 408.5 kJ/kg; η = 62.5%; MEP = 8.52 bar. */
