/* book Worked example 2: Q: A four-cylinder four-stroke petrol engine has a bore of 80 mm and a stroke of 90 mm and runs at 3000 rpm. Its air standard cycle is the Otto cycle of the worked example in Otto, Diesel and Dual cycles (r = 8, 800 kJ/kg added, wnet = 451.8 kJ/kg). Find the MEP and the air standard power.
   1. MEP: v₁ − v₂ = 0.861 − 0.1076 = 0.7534 m³/kg, so pm = 451.8/0.7534 = 599.7 kPa, about 6.0 bar. The closed formula with rp = 48.09/18.38 = 2.617 gives the same 599 kPa.
   2. Swept volume of one cylinder: Vs = (π/4) × 0.08² × 0.09 = 4.524 × 10⁻⁴ m³.
   3. Cycles per second per cylinder (four-stroke): 3000/120 = 25.
   4. Power = 599.7 × 4.524 × 10⁻⁴ × 25 × 4 = 27.1 kW.
   Answer: MEP = 6.0 bar; air standard power = 27.1 kW. The engine's real indicated power is lower, because the real cycle has a smaller area than the air standard loop. */
