/* book exam traps: MEP uses the swept volume v₁ − v₂, not v₁. Dividing 680.8 by 0.861 gives 7.91 bar instead of 8.52 bar. | In a four-stroke engine the number of cycles per minute is N/2, not N. Using N doubles the power. | "Otto is more efficient than Diesel" is true only for the same compression ratio and heat input. For the same peak pressure the order reverses. State the basis before you compare. | During constant-pressure heat addition the temperature keeps rising. The Diesel cycle loses at equal r because it ends its heat addition at a larger entropy, so it rejects more heat, not because the gas cools. | A higher efficiency does not mean a higher MEP. The Carnot cycle has the highest efficiency and one of the lowest MEPs. */
